.TH SHOAL-LANDLOCK-HELPER 1 "July 2026" "Shoal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shoal-landlock-helper \- probe Shoal Landlock enforcement
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shoal-landlock-helper
.I allowed_path denied_path
.SH DESCRIPTION
Internal installation diagnostic used by Shoal Doctor.
It applies a read sandbox, then proves ALLOWED_PATH remains readable and DENIED_PATH does not.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print the probe contract and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
Produces no output on a successful probe; callers interpret the exit status.
.SH ERRORS
Usage, unavailable enforcement, allowed-read failure, and failed denial have distinct statuses.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
shoal-landlock-helper ./allowed.txt ./denied.txt
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 64 for invalid usage, 77 when enforcement is unavailable,
2 when ALLOWED_PATH cannot be read, and 3 when DENIED_PATH remains readable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shoal-doctor (1),
.BR shoal-sandbox-exec (1)
